Chris Holmqvist, cunningly disguised as infinitum@chello.se wrote:

> Then while I'm at it, what are the major differences between the three
> alignments? I've noticed only one thing basically: that more people
> don't attack you when you're lawful, heh.

Actually, not exactly so.

Monsters have a good chance of being peaceful if they are intelligent and
have the same alignment or race as you do. For example, if you're lawful,
chances are that you're playing a dwarfish character. Dwarves and gnomes
are lawful, so the main population of the Gnomish Mines will be peaceful
towards you.

If you are around dungeon level 7 or 8, most creatures created are
animals, which will hardly ever be peaceful, since they're not
intelligent. The only intelligent creatures you'll often encounter there
are centaurs, which won't be peaceful if you're lawful, since most of
these aren't lawful, if I recall correctly.

